                  <comment text="// cancelled tasks are never executed, but may"/>
                  <comment text="// accumulate in work queues, which may causes a memory leak"/>
                  <comment text="// if the task hold references (to an enclosing class for example)"/>
                  <comment text="// we can use purge() but one caveat applies: if a second thread attempts to add"/>
                  <comment text="// something to the pool (suing the execute() method) at the same time the"/>
                  <comment text="// first thread is attempting to purge the queue the attempt to purge"/>
                  <comment text="// the queue fails and the cancelled object remain in the queue."/>
                  <comment text="// A better way to cancel objects with thread pools is to use the remove()"/>
